<<
/Title (respawn prematurely. Automation on the server saw major adjustments; while the restrictive Caps Lock penalty and the automated tips system were entirely removed, new daily automated messages and smart reminders for the !work, !crime, and !hustle commands were introduced. Additionally, language errors across the Shop and Crafting interfaces were fully corrected, the performance of the Mi Fuego system was enhanced, and an essential time converter tool was integrated into the BrainlyHQ Data spreadsheet.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1466 0 R
/Next 1471 0 R
>>
endobj
1471 0 obj
<<
/Title (The economic and gamification loops experienced a complete overhaul to deliver a deeper user experience. A brand-new "Luxury Goods" category was introduced to the shop alongside adjusted prices, distinct separation for the American BrainlyPlus subscription, increased high-level rewards, and a new daily free reward system. Progression and gameplay mechanics were further enriched by modifying the XP system, deploying a sound panel, introducing two new slot machines, and rolling out a Piggy Bank prototype. Additionally, custom pins were introduced alongside visual updates to the users' backpack displays. To support these updates, the process of implementing comprehensive changes to the official drop rates and economy documentation was also initiated. Furthermore, the Science Scavengers drop rates and box configurations were fine-tuned with three new chests, adjusted prices, and randomized odds. Finally, the server embraced a wave of summer features, debuting the Fruit Fever initiative with a 15-exotic-fruit box, "Juicer" workshop mechanics, and powerful economic modifiers such as Coin Rain 4X, Fast Boost 9XP, and two brand-new scratch cards.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1470 0 R
/Next 1467 0 R
>>
endobj
